Default React behavior: parent re-render → all children re-render, even if props same.

Fixes:
- Wrap child in `React.memo` → skip re-render when props shallow-equal.
- Props still change each render? Memo useless. Inline objects, arrays, functions = new ref every render. Stabilize with `useMemo` (objects/arrays), `useCallback` (functions).
- `children` prop as JSX also new ref each parent render. Hoist or memoize.
- Context value change re-render all consumers regardless of `memo`. Memoize provider value, or split contexts.

```jsx
const Child = React.memo(function Child({ onSave, config }) { /* ... */ });

function Parent() {
  const onSave = useCallback(() => { /* ... */ }, []);
  const config = useMemo(() => ({ mode: 'x' }), []);
  return <Child onSave={onSave} config={config} />;
}
```

Verify cause: React DevTools Profiler, enable "Record why each component rendered".

Note: React Compiler (if enabled) auto-memoizes, so manual `memo`/`useMemo` often unneeded.

Default React behavior: parent re-render = child re-render, even if props same. React not compare props unless told.

Fixes:
- Wrap child in `React.memo`: shallow-compare props, skip render if same.
- Props must be stable. Inline object, array, function = new ref each render, breaks `memo`.
  - Objects/arrays: `useMemo`
  - Functions: `useCallback`
- Context change also re-render consumers regardless of `memo`.
- `children` prop from parent JSX = new ref each parent render. Memoize it or lift state down.

```jsx
const Child = React.memo(function Child({ onClick, config }) { /* ... */ });

function Parent() {
  const onClick = useCallback(() => {}, []);
  const config = useMemo(() => ({ a: 1 }), []);
  return <Child onClick={onClick} config={config} />;
}
```

Note: React Compiler (if enabled) auto-memoize, so manual hooks often unneeded.

Still re-render? Share component code + how parent pass props. Check with React DevTools Profiler "Why did this render?".
